    "theory": {
      "summary": "Iconic 16-bar Baroque two-voice minuet in G Major contrasting leaps of a fifth with stepwise 8th-note runs.",
      "pattern_tip": "Notice bars 1-4 and 9-12 share the exact same opening sequence, differing only in the cadence (bars 7-8 half cadence vs. bars 15-16 authentic cadence).",
      "technique_tip": "Articulate the quarter-note leaps gently detached while keeping the four 8th notes smooth and vocal.",
      "ballade_link": "Baroque two-voice independence frees your left hand from pure block chords into melodic counterpoint."
    }
  },
